# Official Documentation First

## Core Principle

Always use the latest official documentation as the primary source when developing with any technology in this project.

Do not rely on outdated knowledge, deprecated APIs, old tutorials, or third-party articles when official documentation is available.

Source priority:

1. Latest official documentation
2. Official GitHub repository
3. Official release notes / changelog
4. Official migration guides
5. Trusted community resources
6. Personal knowledge or assumptions

---

# Identify the Technology Stack

Before implementing a feature, inspect the project to identify frameworks, libraries, languages, runtime/dependency versions, database, and build tools.

Check: `pom.xml`, `package.json`, `docker-compose.yml`, configuration files. Always use the versions actually declared by the project.

